# Allowlist build context (build from repo root): ONLY what games2/Dockerfile
# COPYs. New top-level domains stay out of the context (and off the deploy
# critical path) until the Dockerfile actually bakes them in.
*
!games2
# The maintainer's hand-drawn SOURCE art (5.6 MB): build INPUTS for the bake
# scripts, which are run offline and commit their output — the Dockerfile
# never invokes them and nothing serves ui-src, so every image carried it for
# nothing. The bakes it produces (client/public/ui2) ship as they always did.
# — games-ui 2026-09-03
games2/client/ui-src
games2/node_modules
games2/client/dist
games2/**/*.tsbuildinfo
games2/.data
!scenery
!characters2
!maps2
# ...but NOT the authored BASE the_game is built from (maps2/source/): the
# pipeline's input, 850 KB, read by no consumer at runtime and listed as no
# world. It lives here because the world@1/@2 retirement deleted it and took
# the ability to rebuild the_game with it.
maps2/source
# ...nor the QA render. render3 writes TWO pictures of the_game: the map
# the game shows (minimap.webp / overview.webp, 1200 px, 164 KB) and
# overview_full.webp, the 16300x7576 / 15 MB render this domain reviews the
# world in. The HUD's map tab used to fetch the big one and scale it into a
# frame a few hundred px wide, on a phone (maintainer 2026-09-06).
maps2/worlds3/*/overview_full.webp
!sounds
!music
# AUDIO IS OGG/OPUS ONLY (2026-09-09) — no second format, and no master left
# to exclude. Kept as a standing guard: if the music pipeline ever writes a wav
# beside its ogg again, it must not reach players.
#
# sounds/ IS STILL DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED, for a better reason than before.
# The five takes that used to be wav-only are ogg now: they were not damaged,
# they carried a DC OFFSET (hit_taken_melon rode at +0.5018) and the gate had
# no lower band edge, so it read opus stripping inaudible DC as a 13 dB loss.
# With the band floored at 20 Hz all five encode transparently. The library is
# 100% ogg — so a wav appearing here again means a conversion genuinely FAILED
# and the master is the only copy, which is exactly the case that must still
# reach players. Excluding it would turn a failure into silence.
music/**/*.wav
!monsters
!items
# Tiles 3.0 (/tiles) — THE tile system (tiles2 retired 2026-09-09). The image
# carries only the published world's resolver closure, baked by
# games2/scripts/ship-tiles3.ts in the Dockerfile's build stage; the raw
# candidate sheets in tiles/matrix are gitignored and never enter the context.
!tiles
!lore
!wiki
!live
# ...but NOT the perf telemetry. The client beacon appends to
# live/telemetry/perf.json every 30 s of play (99 commits in one day) and the
# server WRITES it through the GitHub API and never reads it from disk; the
# baked live/ copy exists only as the boot fallback for tuning/ and feedback/.
# Yet it sat in the build context, so EVERY deploy found the curate stage's
# inputs changed and re-ran shipset (49 s), re-copied the repo into /full
# (19 s) and rebuilt the wiki registry (7 s) — 75 s of cache misses per deploy
# for a file nothing in the image uses. Measured on run 3274, 2026-09-09.
live/telemetry
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
*.log
